WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.780
Stretch has to become electrical current somewhere.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.280
Which channel does that, and how would a deletion show it?

3
00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:11.423
This is the second question.

4
00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:15.303
Deleting a channel tests whether the reflex needs it.

5
00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:18.303
Showing that it converts force to current needs recordings.

6
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.667
Force can open a mechanosensitive channel.

7
00:00:22.587 --> 00:00:27.147
Inward current depolarizes the terminal, and if it reaches threshold the afferent

8
00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:28.147
fires.

9
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:33.810
Deleting Piezo2 in adult mouse sensory neurons impaired the lung inflation reflex.

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.980
And driving Piezo2-positive vagal neurons with light caused apnoea.

11
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.760
That uses Piezo2 as a handle.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.770
The artery was harder.

13
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.030
The baroreflex is the reflex by which a rise in blood pressure slows the heart.

14
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:52.993
Channels were deleted from nodose and petrosal neurons.

15
00:00:53.913 --> 00:00:57.093
Blood pressure was raised with a drug in anaesthetized mice.

16
00:00:57.733 --> 00:01:03.373
Deleting Piezo one alone: no statistically detectable difference against littermate

17
00:01:03.373 --> 00:01:04.373
controls.

18
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:09.123
Deleting Piezo two alone: no statistically detectable difference either.

19
00:01:12.716 --> 00:01:16.336
Deleting both essentially abolished the drug-evoked baroreflex.

20
00:01:17.156 --> 00:01:21.756
The magnitude of its sensitivity fell from about five to under one beat per minute

21
00:01:21.756 --> 00:01:23.176
per millimetre of mercury.

22
00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:28.876
in conscious double knockouts, blood pressure in the active period was higher than

23
00:01:28.876 --> 00:01:29.876
in controls.

24
00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:34.526
The tempting reading is that every baroreceptor neuron carries both channels.

25
00:01:35.786 --> 00:01:38.366
Predict. Does that follow from these three rows?

26
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.140
It does not follow.

27
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.040
Either picture could fit, if the input that remains can hold the reflex up.

28
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:55.950
One possible explanation is a nonlinear relation between sensory input and the

29
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.590
reflex. This curve is a hypothesis, not a measurement.

30
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.030
On this chosen curve, halving the input costs one point two three.

31
00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.250
An illustrative cutoff is one point four one.

32
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.410
Neither number tells you what the real experiment could detect.

33
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.770
Losing all of it goes to zero on the curve, and the measured drop is easy to see.

34
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.800
So the experiment shows a collective channel requirement.

35
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.460
It does not measure summed current, or prove coexpression inside a cell.

36
00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:32.373
Separating them needs identified baroreceptors.

37
00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:37.693
Measure channel expression and mechanosensitive current cell by cell, under

38
00:02:37.693 --> 00:02:39.473
controlled mechanical stimulation.

39
00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:44.073
The channels are required collectively in the targeted population.

40
00:02:44.973 --> 00:02:47.673
The result does not show that each neuron carries both.
